 00466
 00467         * due to compiler bug (in ANSI MVT COBOL compiler)
 00468         * we can't have versions in value clause because
 00469         * the compiler doesn't like really big (but valid) numbers
 00470         * in value clauses. they seem ok in moves, computes, ...
 00471          01  KIK-V1                          PIC S9(8) COMP VALUE +0.
 00472          01  KIK-V2                          PIC S9(8) COMP VALUE +0.
